    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-27a7fba53d18\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"to-sign-nonzero-output-value\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"[tT]o_?[sS]ign\\\\w*\\\\.(add_?[oO]utput|AddTxOut)\\\\(.*\\\\bvalue\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[1-9]\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**\"}],\" coverage\":\"\",\"coverage\":\"Flags an added line that calls an output-adding method (addOutput, add_output, AddTxOut) on a to_sign/toSign variable with a nonzero literal value on that same line. The rule requires exactly one zero-value output, so such a call is a flagrant breach.\",\"residual\":\"Setting aside a single-line nonzero-value output added directly to to_sign, does the hunk build the BIP-322 to_sign transaction with a non-OP_RETURN or nonzero-value output, more than one output, or an input that does not spend output 0 of the computed to_spend txid?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/bip322/sign.ts b/src/bip322/sign.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/bip322/sign.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function buildToSign(toSign: any, opReturn: Buffer): void {\\n+  toSign.addOutput({ script: opReturn, value: 546 });\\n+}\\n\"},\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/bip322/sign.ts b/src/bip322/sign.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/bip322/sign.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function buildToSign(toSign: any, opReturn: Buffer): void {\\n+  toSign.addOutput({ script: opReturn, value: 0 });\\n+}\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Most of the rule needs semantic analysis. That includes the output count across several lines, whether the script is OP_RETURN, and whether the input's txid equals the computed to_spend hash. Variable roles also matter. Only a single-line nonzero literal value added to a to_sign-named transaction is mechanically decidable, so the rule is partial.\"}",
